---
import AffiliateDisclosure from './AffiliateDisclosure.astro';
import ComparisonTable from './ComparisonTable.astro';
import GscNotreChoixCompact from './GscNotreChoixCompact.astro';
import { BEST_PROGRAMMABLE_ROBOT_ANGLO } from '../data/bestProgrammableRobotAnglo.mjs';

interface Props {
	marketKey: 'us' | 'uk' | 'ca';
}

const { marketKey } = Astro.props;
const c = BEST_PROGRAMMABLE_ROBOT_ANGLO[marketKey];
const p = c.prefix;
---

<AffiliateDisclosure locale="en" />

<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
	<a href={p}>Home</a> · <a href={`${p}buying-guides/`}>Buying guides</a> · Programmable robots
</nav>
<p>
	<a href={`${p}buying-guides/`}>All buying guides</a> ·{' '}
	<a href={`${p}educational-robot-christmas-gifts-2026/`}>Christmas robot gifts 2026</a> ·{' '}
	<a href={`${p}mbot-vs-mbot2/`}>mBot vs mBot2</a>
</p>

<p>
	<strong>Updated {c.updated}.</strong>
	<Fragment set:html={c.intro} /> Browse our <a href={`${p}buying-guides/`}>buying guides index</a> for age-specific detail
	pages. <strong>Scratch</strong> means block coding (like puzzle pieces); <strong>Arduino</strong> is text-based C/C++ on a
	microcontroller board.
</p>

<GscNotreChoixCompact pageKey="hub-best-robot" market={c.market} locale="en" />

<ComparisonTable
	market={c.market}
	locale="en"
	title="Quick comparison (ages 5–14)"
	products={[
		{ id: 'botley-2', badge: 'Best 5–7 years' },
		{ id: 'mbot', badge: 'Best 8–12 years' },
		{ id: 'mbot2', badge: 'Best 10–14 years' },
		{ id: 'codey-rocky', badge: 'Scratch + sensors' },
		{ id: 'elegoo-robot-car', badge: 'Teen Arduino' },
	]}
/>

<figure>
	<img
		src="/images/products/mbot2.webp"
		alt="Makeblock mBot2 programmable robot with ultrasonic sensors"
		width="600"
		height="600"
		loading="lazy"
		decoding="async"
	/>
</figure>

<h2>Christmas and birthday gifts: practical tips</h2>
<ul>
	<li>
		Match the kit to the child’s <strong>real age and patience</strong>, not the box art — use our{' '}
		<a href={`${p}best-robot-for-an-8-year-old/`}>8-year</a>, <a href={`${p}best-robot-for-a-10-year-old/`}>10-year</a> and{' '}
		<a href={`${p}best-robot-for-a-12-year-old/`}>12-year</a> guides.
	</li>
	<li>
		Charge batteries and install <a href={`${p}install-mblock-5-windows/`}>mBlock 5</a> before unwrapping day so the first session is not
		spent waiting on drivers.
	</li>
	{c.giftBullets.map((b) => (
		<li set:html={b} />
	))}
</ul>

<h2>1. Match the robot to the child, not the marketing</h2>
<ul>
	<li>
		<strong>{marketKey === 'us' ? '5–7 years' : marketKey === 'uk' ? 'Ages 5–7' : 'Grades 1–3'}</strong> — {c.ageBullets.young}; see our{' '}
		<a href={`${p}best-robot-for-a-6-year-old/`}>screen-free coding toys</a>.
	</li>
	<li><strong>{marketKey === 'us' ? '8–10 years' : marketKey === 'uk' ? 'Ages 8–10' : 'Grades 4–6'}</strong> — {c.ageBullets.mid}.</li>
	<li><strong>{marketKey === 'us' ? '10–14 years' : marketKey === 'uk' ? 'Ages 10–14' : 'Grades 7–8'}</strong> — {c.ageBullets.older}.</li>
	<li><strong>{marketKey === 'us' ? '13+ with an adult' : marketKey === 'uk' ? 'Ages 13+ with an adult' : 'Secondary + adult helper'}</strong> — {c.ageBullets.teen}.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Three criteria that matter</h2>
<p>
	<strong>Software still maintained</strong> (tutorials, community), <strong>at least two types of challenge</strong> (line follow,
	obstacle, light…), and <strong>total budget</strong> including batteries and storage. If you choose Makeblock, start with{' '}
	<a href={`${p}install-mblock-5-windows/`}>installing mBlock 5 on Windows</a>.
</p>

<h2>Manufacturer specs (reference)</h2>
<p set:html={c.specsLead} />

<div class="tableau empile">
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th scope="col">Criterion</th>
				<th scope="col">mBot</th>
				<th scope="col">mBot2</th>
				<th scope="col">ELEGOO Robot Car V4.0</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td data-label="Criterion">
					<span class="td-val">Stated age</span>
				</td>
				<td data-label="mBot">
					<span class="td-val">6+</span>
				</td>
				<td data-label="mBot2">
					<span class="td-val">{c.specAgeMbot2}</span>
				</td>
				<td data-label="ELEGOO Robot Car V4.0">
					<span class="td-val">13+ with an adult helper</span>
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td data-label="Criterion">
					<span class="td-val">Languages</span>
				</td>
				<td data-label="mBot">
					<span class="td-val">Blocks (mBlock), Arduino</span>
				</td>
				<td data-label="mBot2">
					<span class="td-val">Blocks, Python, Arduino IDE on CyberPi</span>
				</td>
				<td data-label="ELEGOO Robot Car V4.0">
					<span class="td-val">Arduino (C/C++)</span>
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td data-label="Criterion">
					<span class="td-val">Assembly time</span>
				</td>
				<td data-label="mBot">
					<span class="td-val">~15 minutes</span>
				</td>
				<td data-label="mBot2">
					<span class="td-val">~30 minutes</span>
				</td>
				<td data-label="ELEGOO Robot Car V4.0">
					<span class="td-val">Modular XH2.54 connectors</span>
				</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>
</div>

<h2>3. Age guides on this site</h2>
<p>
	<a href={`${p}best-robot-for-an-8-year-old/`}>Robot for 8 years</a> · <a href={`${p}best-robot-for-a-10-year-old/`}>10 years</a> ·{' '}
	<a href={`${p}best-robot-for-a-12-year-old/`}>12 years</a> · <a href={`${p}mbot-vs-mbot2/`}>mBot vs mBot2</a> ·{' '}
	<a href={`${p}makeblock-brand/`}>Makeblock brand hub</a>
</p>

<h2>Common mistakes</h2>
<ul>
	<li>Buying the cheapest kit with {c.mistakeDoc}.</li>
	<li>Underestimating adult time for drivers, Bluetooth and first login.</li>
	<li>Choosing a teen Arduino kit for a 7-year-old who still prefers play without a laptop.</li>
</ul>

<p>
	<strong>In short:</strong> the best robot is the one that will actually be used — clear software, varied challenges, honest budget. Start
	from an age guide, then {c.closing}.
</p>